The XSD and Schematron retain the cinematic extensions below; they are not byte-identical
to the upstream files. The capability JSON Schema is vendored unchanged. Local XML filenames
retain 1.1 for tooling compatibility. SREP 57 generated markers, SREP 59 reference checks
and SREP 63 conditional capability entries are implemented. The former pending SREPs
16, 17, 18, 19, 21 and 26 are implemented; PDF resolution requires the pdf build feature.

Added here, not in sr-core 1.3.0 (SREP 0 of this repository, the cinematic proposal, srep-0000-cinematic-impact.md):
the elements blackHole and accretionDisk (blackHoleType, accretionDiskType; rules BH1 to BH8), camera/@geodesics,
fracture/@source, fracture/@minImpulse and fracture/@energyFraction (rules FRX5 to FRX7), ocean/@density, crater/@mantle,
crater/@bulking and crater/@repose (rules CRT10 to CRT12), and pyro/@follow, @followMargin and @followLoss (rules PYRO9 to
PYRO11); the
rest of the cinematic families (OCN, P3D, CRT, PYC, PYRO, VOL, FRX, MSQ, GEO) is in sr-core 1.3.0 as released. A
release of sr-core that takes these in replaces them; until then a vendoring keeps them (the merge of
2026-10-06 was done by component: every top-level type, group and pattern that sr-core changed since the previous
vendoring is theirs, every one that only this repository changed is ours, and nothing was changed by both).

Local addition ahead of an sr-core release: document version 1.6 (scene/@version gains "1.6"; sr_model::SCHEMA_VERSION
is "1.6"), with no 1.6 syntax. It is the base on which the branches of the SREPs accepted on 2026-10-09 (66 to 75) add
their own syntax and version rules; a 1.6 document holding 1.5 content validates and renders as the same document at
1.5. The capability manifest still names the vendored release 1.5.0. A vendoring of sr-core 1.6.0 replaces this.

Added here ahead of an sr-core release: SREP 67 (accepted 2026-10-09). This covers compute, iterate and tonemap
(computeType, densityTonemapType, iterateType), the effect types error-diffusion and segmented-sort with their attributes,
and the Schematron pattern p-srep67 (V13, ITR1, ITR2, SRT1). Three local differences from the SREP's text exist because
of the model generator of sr-model:
- computeType's content is a choice instead of the sequence (param*, tonemap?, behaviour*), with CMP13 keeping one
  tonemap at most;
- the union of tonemap/@reference is named densityReferenceType;
- its keyword is named densityReferenceKeyword.
Every document valid under the SREP is valid here.
